Package: iphone-mirror-bridge
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: abrham8 <abrham8@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-dbus, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gir1.2-gst-plugins-base-1.0, python3-gst-1.0, python3-evdev, bluez, uxplay, avahi-daemon, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-libav, gstreamer1.0-gl, python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, python3-pyside6.qtqml, python3-pyside6.qtquick, python3-pyside6.qtnetwork, qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-window, qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-effects, qml6-module-qtquick-controls, qml6-module-qtquick-templates, qml6-module-qtqml-workerscript, qt6-svg-plugins, qt6-wayland, fonts-inter
Recommends: libnotify-bin
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/abrham8/iphone-mirror-bridge
Description: see and control your iPhone from Linux
 iPhone Mirror Bridge shows the iPhone's screen in a window on the computer
 (AirPlay, via UxPlay) and makes the computer act as a Bluetooth mouse and
 keyboard for the iPhone. With AssistiveTouch enabled, the laptop touchpad
 moves the iPhone pointer, clicks, scrolls and drags, and the keyboard types.
 Click the mirrored screen to take control; Ctrl+F8 switches back.
 .
 The desktop app has a system tray icon, a pairing window that shows the
 6-digit Bluetooth code, and settings for display and controls.
